-- title:
--   Divisor specialisation preserves degree zero and principality
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$, a prime $\ell$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $k_A = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ has characteristic $\ell$, and assume $\ell \nmid N$. Let `fm` be a `FibreModel` for $N$, $A$, $\ell$, $k_A$ and the residue map $A \to k_A$: that is, a pair of subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$N$ modular function field inside Laurent series, each containing the image of $A$ under `constantsHom`, with $\bar{j}, \bar{j}_N \in B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\bar{j}^{-1} \in B_{\mathrm{inf}}$, each integral over the corresponding affine chart base ring, together with ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}, \pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ to $k_A(\bar{j},\bar{j}_N) =$ `modularFunctionFieldC` $k_A\,N$ reducing constants through the residue map and sending $\bar{j}, \bar{j}_N, \bar{j}^{-1}$ to the expected elements. Let `cc` be a `CuspChart` for `fm`, i.e. a witness that $\bar{j}_N \cdot (\bar{j}^{-1})^N$ lies in $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ and that $\pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ sends it to $j_N \cdot j^{-N}$ in the special fibre. Let `dataAll` assign to every divisor $d$ of $N$ a `ModularPolynomialData` $d$, namely a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(d)$ with $\Phi(j, j_d) = 0$, and let `hsep` assert that the image of $\Phi$ for $d = N$ in $\mathrm{RatFunc}(k_A)[Y]$ is separable. Assume further the predicate [`ModularCurve.ReductionInputsModL`](def/ModularCurve_ReductionModL.html#L184) $A\,N$ (whose content used here is that the principal divisors of the function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lie in the subgroup generated by [`ModularCurve.integralPrincipalDivisors`](def/ModularCurve_ReductionModL.html#L30) $A$ (residue $A$) $N$), and that $k_A(\bar{j},\bar{j}_N)$ coincides with `modularFunctionFieldFullC` $k_A\,N$, the subfield generated by all divisor expansions. Then `fm.SpDivPreservesPrincipal` holds: the pushforward `fm.spDiv` of divisors along the specialisation map of places sends every degree-zero divisor on the function field `modularFunctionFieldBar` $N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to a degree-zero divisor on $k_A(\bar{j},\bar{j}_N)$, and sends every degree-zero principal divisor (one of the form $v \mapsto \mathrm{ord}_v f$ for some $f \neq 0$) to a principal divisor.
--
--   This is the statement that reduction of divisors from $X_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to its special fibre at a residue characteristic $\ell \nmid N$ is compatible with degrees and with linear equivalence, in the form in which good reduction enters through Deuring's reduction of places. It is used in the construction of place specialisations for fibre models of $X_0(N)$ and in the production of specialisations with good reduction at $j = 0$.
